WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.575
Once policies are on, the
sign-in logs are the instrument.

2
00:00:03.575 --> 00:00:06.838
The queries run against the
SigninLogs table in a Log

3
00:00:06.838 --> 00:00:10.175
Analytics workspace that
receives Entra sign-in logs.

4
00:00:10.175 --> 00:00:11.838
The chapter gives them in full;

5
00:00:11.838 --> 00:00:16.230
they're illustrative and haven't been
tested against a production workspace, so

6
00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:18.692
confirm column values
against your own data

7
00:00:18.692 --> 00:00:21.087
before using them for
alerting or evidence.

8
00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:22.562
Six signals matter.

9
00:00:22.562 --> 00:00:27.587
Per-policy results over seven days, including
report-only outcomes; after wave two,

10
00:00:27.587 --> 00:00:30.173
members of the Admins group should show no

11
00:00:30.173 --> 00:00:33.425
not-applied results for
the administrator policies.

12
00:00:33.425 --> 00:00:38.228
Blocked sign-ins, error 53003, which
is blocked by Conditional Access;

13
00:00:38.228 --> 00:00:42.020
a spike on a single application
usually means a client

14
00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:45.812
that can't do modern
authentication or app protection.

15
00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:51.262
The end-state gap: users who would
fail CA022 while it's in report-only.

16
00:00:51.262 --> 00:00:54.138
That's the list that drives
the enrollment campaign.

17
00:00:54.138 --> 00:00:58.440
Legacy authentication still
in use, over fourteen days,

18
00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:01.901
which must be empty
before CA001 is enforced.

19
00:01:01.901 --> 00:01:06.189
Coverage gaps: successful sign-ins
that no policy applied to,

20
00:01:06.189 --> 00:01:10.650
which should be empty for interactive
sign-ins once CA018 is on.

21
00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:13.879
And emergency account use,
matched on object IDs,

22
00:01:13.879 --> 00:01:17.350
which should be zero outside
scheduled validation.

23
00:01:17.350 --> 00:01:18.313
Then drift.

24
00:01:18.313 --> 00:01:22.769
The policy set in the tenant must
equal the policy set in source control,

25
00:01:22.769 --> 00:01:27.680
and the drift check alerts on a policy
whose state changed without an approved

26
00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:30.929
change; a change to any
exclusion group's membership,

27
00:01:30.929 --> 00:01:35.915
especially the emergency access group;
a change to conditions, named locations,

28
00:01:35.915 --> 00:01:38.408
authentication strengths or controls;

29
00:01:38.408 --> 00:01:41.505
a policy created or deleted
outside the pipeline,

30
00:01:41.505 --> 00:01:45.963
including a Microsoft-managed policy
that Microsoft added or enabled;

31
00:01:45.963 --> 00:01:50.312
and users or devices missing the
attributes that put them in scope.

32
00:01:50.312 --> 00:01:54.893
Protected actions, which require
fresh strong authentication to change

33
00:01:54.893 --> 00:01:59.550
policies and named locations, narrow
who can cause drift in the first place.

34
00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:01.320
Module three builds them.
